      ":question/id": "ac23880f-9ba9-56b5-be16-154f1b3ed098",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x+21y+14z &=35 \\\\ 9x-27y-18z &=-45 \\\\ x-3y-2z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-7 & 21 & 14 & 35 \\\\ 9 & -27 & -18 & -45 \\\\ 1 & -3 & -2 & -5\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\nR_1\\leftrightarrow R_3\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 9 & -27 & -18 & -45 \\\\ -7 & 21 & 14 & 35\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_2:=R_2+(-9)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 21 & 14 & 35\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nR_3:=R_3+(7)R_1\n$$\n\n\n\n$$\nM\\sim \\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & -3 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\n",
